RTL Coding Guidelines for Better Performance
With X-Propagation
This document explains the RTL coding guidelines that provides improved compile and
runtime performance.
This document includes the following sections:
• Encoding Large Multiplexers
• Loops With Flow Control
• Functions With Multiple Return Statement
Encoding Large Multiplexers
You must encode large multiplexers using the case construct. You should avoid deeply
nested-if statements as the performance becomes lower. The nested-if statement leads to
more evaluations compared to case construct.
The following is the recommended coding style:
always_comb begin
case(sel)
0: out = in0;
1: out = in1;
2: out = in2;
//Code Pruned
127: out = in127;
endcase
end
end
Loops With Flow Control
By default, Xprop does not instrument loop containing break/continue in Verilog or exit/
next in VHDL. You can perform instrumentation using the -xprop=flowctrl option. However,
instrumenting these statements have some performance implications. As an indeterminate
