The assert_frame checker validates proper
timing, cycle checker
cycle timing relationships between two
events in the design. When a start_event evaluates true, then the test_expr must
evaluate true within a minimum and maximum number of clock cycles.
assert_frame [#( severity_level, min_cks, max_cks, flag,
inst_name ( clk, reset_n, start_event, test_expr );
min_cks
Minimum number of clock cycles, within which the test_expr should not become true.
When min_cks is 0 then test_expr can occur at the same time as start_event or after as
controlled by max_cks. Default = 0.
max_cks
Maximum number of clock cycles, before which test_expr must become true. This check is
disabled when max_cks is not specified, that is, when min_cks > 0 and max_cks == 0. If
both min_cks and max_cks are 0 then test_expr must occur at the same time as there is a
0 to 1 transition on start_event. Default = 0.
flag
0 - Ignores any asserted start_event after the first one has been detected (default);

