Parameterizing a Subplan
When you instantiate a subplan, attribute values can be passed to the subplan as follows:
subplan cache_plan #(root_mod="memsys_test_top.dut.u0.");
Here, the root_mod attributes is set to the instance path of a block.
This parameter-passing technique can be used to enable or disable feature groups. This
technique uses a negative polarity , in which you disable the feature groups that are
not required. If you do not turn off a feature group, you may get poor coverage for the
unused feature group. You can also implement this same technique with a positive polarity,
that is, turning on the required feature groups. If you use the positive approach, you may
have the risk of missing verification holes by not turning on a feature group that you are
using in your design.
Feature groups are a group of Hierarchical Verification Plan (HVP) features and may be

).)*attribute-identifer

annotation-full-identifier ::= plan-identifier.((plan- identifer |
feature_identifer).)*annotation-identifer

)*attribute-identifer

annotation-full-identifier ::= plan-identifier.((plan- identifer |
feature_identifer).)*annotation-identifer

metric-full-identifier ::= plan-identifier.((plan- identifer |
feature_identifer).)*metric-identifer
The following is an example using override to change the goal of Line coverage for
myplan.DVD_RW to be greater than 85%:
override milestone_1;
myplan.DVD_RW.Line = Line > 85%;
An attribute value that is assigned in an override statement is immediately propagated all
the way down to the leaf node features. This means that if you specify an attribute override
statement of a child node followed by the same attribute override of a parent node, the
child node override, specified first, becomes meaningless. However, the same is not
true for annotation overrides because annotation values are not propagated downward.
In the following example, the resulting owner is Second Owner for all instances in the
topplan.subplan1 hierarchy level and below, including the topplan.subplan1.mem
instance.
override ov_owner;
/* change the weight attribute in feature top.feat.mem */
topplan.subplan1.mem.owner = "First Owner";
topplan.subplan1.owner = "Second Owner";
