-negdelay:flexfanout
Limits negative interconnect delay handling to fan-out paths only. Use this option with
-negdelay when fan-out-only adjustment is required.
With the default -negdelay algorithm, when VCS encounters a negative
INTERCONNECT delay, it first attempts to resolve the negative delay from fan-out paths. If
fan-out adjustment is not possible, VCS attempts to resolve the negative delay from fan-in
paths. When adjusting from fan-in paths, VCS also adjusts all parallel interconnect delays
on those paths. This adjustment of parallel interconnect delays can cause incorrect values
to be sampled in scan tests.
-negdelay:flexfanout prevents fan-in-path adjustment and limits negative delay
handling to fan-out paths only.
With the default algorithm, VCS may skip fan-out-path adjustment when all fan-out paths
are conditional (COND) paths and no CONDELSE path is present. -negdelay:flexfanout
ignores the requirement for a CONDELSE path and does not verify that all conditions are
covered. When only conditional delays are present on fan-out paths, VCS considers the
available conditional delays.
vcs test.v -negdelay -negdelay:flexfanout [other_vcs_options]
vcs test.v -negdelay -negdelay:flexfanout -sdf min:top:design.sdf

In this example, negative INTERCONNECT delays in design.sdf are handled only from
fan-out paths. Fan-in-path adjustment and parallel interconnect delay changes are not
performed.
