-simp_loop_report
The -simp_loop_report=time=<time> option in VCS reports zero-delay infinite loops
during simulation by using simprofile after the loop report is triggered. It helps verify
whether the number of loops exceeds the threshold specified during compile time. The
time is used to set the duration of the simprofiler. It is optional in runtime and its default is
300.
To use the -simp_loop_report, it is mandatory to include the
-simp_loop_report=threshold=<threshold> option at compile time.
When -simp_loop_report=threshold=<threshold> is specified at compile time:
• If -simp_loop_report=time=<time> is specified at runtime, VCS checks whether the
delta-cycle exceeds the specified threshold. If yes, VCS triggers the loop report and
starts the profiler. The profiler works for the specified time and reports the collected
samples.
-simp_loop_report=time=<time>
