input T in2; //implicit port kind, in2 is variable by
//default and net under switch
//"sv_net_ports"
input in3;
T in3; // in3 is variable
output T out;

The use model for this feature is as follows:
1. Net declarations with explicit data type are supported by default in this release.
2. Port declaration with implicit port kind follows the SystemVerilog LRM rules under the
-sv_net_ports option.

Support for Net with Data Types
Changing Default Port Kind
By default, VCS treats input or inout ports with implicit port kind and explicit data type as
variable. However, as per LRM it should be net.
For scalars, vectors, and packed structures or unions, you can use the
-sv_net_ports=packed
-
sv_net_ports=packed option. This option treats ports with implicit port kind and explicit
data type as a net, as specified in LRM Section 23.2.2.3 Rules for determining port kind,
data type, and direction.
• The VCS coverage database (VDBs) generated using the - sv_net_ports=packed
option are not merge compatible with the coverage databases generated without the
• If - sv_net_ports=packed option is added or removed from compile-to-compile, you
must regenerate the coverage exclusion file.
The use model is as follows:
• % vcs -sverilog -sv_net_ports=packed <other_options> <file_name>
• % simv
For diagnostic information, use
–sv_net_ports=diags
-sv_net_ports=diags during compilation.
In VCS three step flow, use either of the following use models:
1. You can pass this option at both vlogan and vcs commands as shown below:
◦ % vlogan -sverilog <file_name> -sv_net_ports=packed
◦ % vcs <top-module> -sv_net_ports=packed
OR
2. You can set the SV_NET_PORTS and SV_NET_PORTS_DIAGS variables in the
synopsys_sim.setup file.
SV_NET_PORTS:
◦ Valid SV_NET_PORTS values are ALL and PACKED.
◦ When set to ALL, VCS treats all input/inout ports with implicit port kind as a net.
◦ When set to PACKED, VCS treats input/inout ports of scalar, vector, packed structure,
packed union types, and implicit port kind as a net.

Support for Net with Data Types
SV_NET_PORTS_DIAGS:
◦ When set to TRUE, VCS prints diagnostic messages for the ports which are treated
as a net.
If you pass the -sv_net_ports option at the command line and also set the
SV_NET_PORTS variable in the synopsys_sim.setup file, the superset option is considered
by VCS.
Consider the following test case, when lowconn is forced, the value propagates to
highconn incase of net.
Example 59 test.v
module m1( input logic [1:0]aa );
#10; $display("%m aa: ",aa);
end
module m2(input logic [1:0]aa);
m1 m1_inst(aa);

