Improved MSV Parameter Override and Optimizations in Verilog-AMS Flow
The parameter vsup of capacitor instance BOT1 has the most common value (1.1) in
module mid.
For the three capacitor instances (top.m1.BOT1, top.m2.BOT1, and top.m3.BOT1),
an optimization is used. The less commonly used parameter value of 2.8 for instance
top.m3.BOT1 is passed using the hierarchical format (explicit assignment), whereas
the more frequently used value of 1.1 for the other two instances (top.m1.BOT1, and
top.m2.BOT1) is passed using the folded format (implicit assignment).
Improved Partitioning for SPICE Primitive and Sub-Circuit
Parameter Values
To optimize partitioning efficiency, VCS handles boundary SPICE parameters using two
distinct methods:
• Folded Format: The most common value of a boundary Spice parameter is passed in a
folded manner through a partition file.
• Flattened Format: Parameter values for all other scenarios are partitioned in a flattened
hierarchical format via a separate partition file.
To enable this feature, use the -adopt sp_param_part_enh compile option.
Consider the following testcases:
Example 103 Top Module
electrical p1, p2;
mid MID(p1, P2);

module mid(p1, p2);
output p1, p2;
electrical p1, p2;
leaf LEAF0(p1, P2);
leaf LEAF1(p1, P2);
leaf #(.rp(6.0)) LEAF2(p1, P2);
leaf #(.rp(8.0)) LEAF3(p1, P2);
Example 104 VAMS Module with Spice Primitive
module leaf (out, gnd);
output out, gnd;
electrical out, gnd;

parameter real r1 = 1.0;
parameter real r2 = 2.0;
parameter real rp = 5.0;

capacitor #(.c(3n)) C3 (b1, gnd);

Improved MSV Parameter Override and Optimizations in Verilog-AMS Flow
capacitor #(.c(1p), .ic(1)) C1 (vcc, out);
capacitor #(.c(r1+r2)) C4 (b1, gnd);
capacitor #(.c(rp)) C5 (b1, gnd);
The parameter vsup of capacitor instance C5 has the most common value (5.0) in
module leaf. This value is passed to the analog simulator as an instance-specific
override for top.MID.LEAF0.C5 and top.MID.LEAF1.C5. For the remaining instances
(top.MID.LEAF2.C5’ and top.MID.LEAF3.C5), the values of the parameter vsup are
passed in hierarchical format.
Improved Partitioning of SPICE Primitive Parameter Values
VCS now generates parameters during elaboration based on overrides specified in
the netlist, rather than using a predefined parameter set within the shadow module
of a Spice primitive. To enable this enhanced parameter handling, use the -adopt
sp_prim_param_enh compile option.
The following example shows Verilog-AMS module containing instances of Spice
primitives:
Example 105 VAMS Module Containing Instances of Spice Primitives
module leaf (out, gnd);
output out, gnd;
electrical out, gnd;

parameter real r1 = 1.0;
parameter real r2 = 2.0;
parameter real rp = 5.0;

capacitor #(.c(3n)) C3 (b1, gnd);
capacitor #(.c(1p), .ic(1)) C1 (vcc, out);
capacitor #(.c(r1+r2)) C4 (b1, gnd);
capacitor #(.c(rp)) C5 (b1, gnd);
